insert into public.quiz_questions
(module_id, question, options, correct_index, explanation, difficulty, is_certification, exam_track)
values
('m1','A new hire is created in Workday, but the identity is not created in Saviynt after the scheduled import. Which investigation sequence is most appropriate?','["Check identity import job status and source connection, inspect rejected records and mandatory attribute mappings, then validate create-user rules","Launch an access certification","Run entitlement import only","Change all user correlation rules to email"]',0,'Start with the authoritative source feed and import execution, inspect rejected rows and required attributes, then validate identity creation and mapping logic.','Intermediate',true,'professional'),
('m2','An account import succeeds, but a large number of accounts are orphaned. Which control should be reviewed first?','["Password policy","Account-to-identity correlation rule and source attribute quality","Certification schedule","Email template"]',1,'Successful ingestion does not guarantee identity correlation. Validate stable keys, normalization, uniqueness and source data quality.','Intermediate',true,'professional'),
('m3','A manager requests access for a direct report. The application owner must approve high-risk entitlements while the manager approves business need. Which workflow design best fits?','["Single approval by requester","Sequential or parallel multi-step approval with entitlement risk-based routing","Auto-approve all requests","Certification-only workflow"]',1,'Use approval stages and routing conditions so business ownership and application risk are both evaluated.','Intermediate',true,'professional'),
('m4','An AD account is created, but group membership provisioning fails. What should be checked first?','["Only the user profile photo","Provisioning task status, connector logs, group DN/identifier, permissions and target connectivity","Delete the identity","Disable all AD imports"]',1,'Trace the failed task from request/workflow through provisioning and connector response; validate the target object identifier and delegated permissions.','Intermediate',true,'professional'),
('m5','A user changes department and should lose old department access while receiving new birthright access. Which lifecycle event is relevant?','["Joiner","Mover","Leaver","Password reset"]',1,'A mover event evaluates changed identity attributes and should trigger access recalculation and removal/addition logic.','Intermediate',true,'professional'),
('m6','A certification reviewer revokes an entitlement. What is the expected governance outcome?','["The entitlement is immediately deleted from the target without a task","A remediation action/task is generated and tracked through completion","The identity is disabled","The reviewer becomes the entitlement owner"]',1,'Revocation decisions must flow to remediation and be tracked until target access is removed or an exception is recorded.','Intermediate',true,'professional'),
('m7','A preventive SoD policy detects a conflict during an access request. When should the conflict be evaluated?','["Only after provisioning","Before approval/provisioning so the request can be blocked or routed for mitigation","Only during annual certification","Only after termination"]',1,'Preventive controls evaluate proposed access before it is granted, allowing rejection or approved mitigating controls.','Intermediate',true,'professional'),
('m8','An entitlement import returns duplicate entitlements because display names are reused across business units. What is the best remediation?','["Use display name as the unique key","Use a stable target-side entitlement identifier and preserve required scope/context","Delete all duplicates manually after every import","Turn off entitlement imports"]',1,'Stable unique identifiers prevent collisions; include scope or parent context where the target system requires it.','Intermediate',true,'professional'),
('m9','A REST connector receives HTTP 401 during account import. Which area should be validated first?','["Pagination size","Authentication configuration, token validity, scopes and credential rotation","Account correlation","Certification reviewer delegation"]',1,'401 indicates authentication failure; validate credential/token acquisition and authorization context before changing import logic.','Intermediate',true,'professional'),
('m10','A provisioning request remains pending although approval is complete. Which evidence best narrows the issue?','["User training completion","Provisioning task state, job execution, connector response and retry/error logs","Number of published lessons","Identity profile biography"]',1,'Separate workflow approval from fulfillment. Inspect the task and provisioning job to determine whether dispatch, connector execution or target response failed.','Intermediate',true,'professional'),
('m11','A business wants contractors to lose access automatically at the end of their engagement. What is the strongest design?','["Rely on managers to remember","Maintain an authoritative end date and trigger time-bound lifecycle deprovisioning","Run a quarterly email reminder only","Give contractors permanent access"]',1,'An authoritative end date enables deterministic lifecycle processing and auditable removal of access.','Intermediate',true,'professional'),
('m12','A JDBC import job is slow and times out on a large target table. What is the best first optimization?','["Remove all filters","Review query plan, indexes, incremental watermark/filtering and fetch/paging strategy","Increase every timeout indefinitely","Import the same table multiple times"]',1,'Optimize the source query and incremental extraction design before relying on larger timeouts.','Intermediate',true,'professional'),
('m13','A REST API uses offset pagination and returns 100 records per page. The import stops after the first page. Which configuration area is likely incomplete?','["Account status mapping","Pagination loop/next-page handling and termination condition","Identity display name","Certification campaign owner"]',1,'The connector must request subsequent pages and stop only when the API indicates no more records.','Intermediate',true,'professional'),
('m14','An access request is approved but the target system rejects the operation because the account is disabled. What should the implementation do?','["Mark the request fulfilled","Surface the target error, keep fulfillment unsuccessful, and route the task for remediation/retry after account state is corrected","Delete the approval history","Automatically approve another request"]',1,'Approval and successful provisioning are separate states; preserve the failure evidence and resolve target prerequisites.','Intermediate',true,'professional'),
('m15','An auditor asks for evidence that a terminated employee no longer has access. Which evidence set is most useful?','["Only a screenshot of the user profile","Leaver event/timestamp, affected accounts and entitlements, provisioning/remediation results, and target confirmation","A list of active lessons","A manager email without system evidence"]',1,'A defensible audit trail connects the authoritative termination event to each target removal and its completion evidence.','Intermediate',true,'professional'),
('m16','A Saviynt implementation team is preparing application onboarding. What should be established before connector configuration?','["Production cutover date only","Application owner, data owners, account/entitlement model, authoritative attributes, access use cases and connectivity prerequisites","Only the logo and application name","Certification campaign email wording"]',1,'Discovery and data analysis define scope, ownership, source-of-truth, access model and technical prerequisites.','Intermediate',true,'professional'),
('m17','A manager cannot see a direct report in a certification campaign. Which data relationship should be checked?','["The manager email template","Identity manager attribute, manager identity correlation and campaign population/filter criteria","The AD password policy","The user's browser cache only"]',1,'Manager certification populations depend on accurate manager relationships and campaign selection logic.','Intermediate',true,'professional'),
('m18','An application owner wants access reviews only for privileged entitlements every month. What is the best approach?','["Review every identity attribute daily","Define a targeted certification population/filter for privileged entitlements and schedule the campaign monthly","Disable certification","Create a new identity for each entitlement"]',1,'Risk-based certification scope reduces reviewer noise while focusing on privileged access.','Intermediate',true,'professional'),
('m19','A connector import is successful in test but fails in production with DNS resolution errors. What is the most relevant first check?','["Question bank configuration","Production runtime network/DNS resolution, hostname, firewall and routing from the connector execution environment","User certification score","Email notification wording"]',1,'Environment-specific name resolution and network path must be validated from the actual execution host.','Intermediate',true,'professional'),
('m20','A role contains entitlements from multiple applications. Which statement best describes an enterprise role?','["It is always a single AD group","It can bundle access across multiple applications to represent a business job function","It replaces identity correlation","It is a certification campaign"]',1,'Enterprise roles aggregate access across systems around a business function, subject to ownership and governance.','Intermediate',true,'professional'),
('m1','A Workday feed delivers a changed employee ID for an existing worker. The next import creates a duplicate identity instead of updating the existing identity. What is the most robust remediation?','["Change correlation to display name","Analyze immutable source identifiers and identity correlation strategy, reconcile the duplicate, then correct source mapping and matching precedence","Delete the new identity and ignore future imports","Disable all identity imports"]',1,'Identity correlation should use stable identifiers and controlled matching precedence. Reconcile duplicates carefully before changing production rules.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m2','An account import from SAP completes, but some accounts correlate to the wrong identities because usernames are reused in different client numbers. What should the correlation key include?','["Username only","A composite stable key including the SAP client/system context and account identifier","Account description","Last login timestamp"]',1,'Account identifiers must be unique in their target namespace. Include system/client context where usernames can repeat.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m3','A REST connector intermittently receives HTTP 429 during entitlement import. Which implementation is most resilient?','["Retry immediately without limit","Implement bounded exponential backoff honoring Retry-After, control concurrency and checkpoint pagination","Treat 429 as an empty successful response","Disable entitlement import permanently"]',1,'Rate-limit-aware retries with backoff and checkpointing reduce repeated throttling and avoid losing pagination progress.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m4','A provisioning workflow succeeds for most AD groups but fails only for nested groups in a specific OU. What is the most targeted investigation?','["Rebuild every endpoint","Compare distinguished names, OU permissions, group scope/nesting behavior and connector operation logs for the failing OU","Change all users to service accounts","Disable group imports"]',1,'Scope the issue to target object structure and delegated permissions; compare successful and failed operations in the affected OU.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m5','A mover event removes old access only after the next full account import. The business requires removal during the same lifecycle cycle. Which design area should be examined?','["Lesson completion rules","Identity change detection, analytics/rule trigger timing, workflow sequencing and provisioning orchestration","Dashboard theme","Quiz pass mark"]',1,'The event-to-action chain must detect the attribute change and sequence access recalculation/removal without waiting for an unrelated full import.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m6','A certification campaign contains 80,000 items and reviewer pages load slowly. Which optimization should be considered without weakening review scope?','["Remove all entitlements from the campaign","Segment campaigns by application/owner/risk, tune population filters and validate data volume and reviewer assignment","Assign every item to one reviewer","Disable audit history"]',1,'Campaign segmentation and precise population design improve workload distribution while preserving required control coverage.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m7','A preventive SoD rule produces false positives because two entitlements share similar names but represent different business actions. What should be improved?','["Increase the pass mark","Use authoritative entitlement identifiers and well-defined function/risk mappings; validate rule conditions with business owners","Disable all SoD checks","Use display-name substring matching only"]',1,'SoD rules should map business functions to stable entitlement identifiers and be validated against real process semantics.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m8','A role-mining exercise proposes hundreds of roles that differ by one low-risk entitlement. What governance response is most appropriate?','["Approve every proposed role","Apply usage thresholds, normalize access patterns, assess business meaningfulness and ownership, and consolidate near-duplicate candidates","Delete all existing roles","Convert every entitlement into a birthright role"]',1,'Role mining is a discovery input, not automatic approval. Consolidate candidates using meaningful job-function patterns and governance criteria.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m9','A JDBC connector query uses a timestamp watermark. Records updated at the exact watermark timestamp are sometimes missed between runs. What is a safer extraction pattern?','["Use a strict greater-than timestamp with no overlap","Use a deterministic composite cursor or overlap window with idempotent upsert/deduplication","Remove ordering from the query","Use random record sampling"]',1,'Timestamp precision and concurrent updates can create gaps. An overlap window or composite cursor plus idempotent processing prevents missed changes.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m10','An SAP password-change operation fails only when passwords contain certain special characters. What should be investigated first?','["Increase the user's role","Payload/JSON escaping, connector parameter encoding and target API password policy; reproduce safely with controlled test values","Disable password policy","Store the password in a log"]',1,'Special-character failures often arise from encoding/escaping or target policy. Never log plaintext credentials; test with controlled secure values.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m11','An application uses SCIM PATCH and returns success, but a multi-valued group attribute is unintentionally overwritten. What is the likely design issue?','["Wrong certification owner","Incorrect PATCH operation/path semantics or replace-vs-add behavior for multi-valued attributes","The identity has no manager","The import schedule is daily"]',1,'SCIM PATCH semantics matter: add, remove and replace operations have different effects on multi-valued attributes. Validate the target behavior.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m12','A leaver has 12 accounts across 6 endpoints. Two endpoints are unavailable during deprovisioning. What is the strongest operational handling?','["Mark all accounts removed","Track each endpoint task independently, retry failed operations, escalate exceptions and retain evidence until every target is resolved","Delete the identity record immediately","Close the ticket after the first successful removal"]',1,'Deprovisioning is multi-target. Maintain per-target status, retry/exception handling and audit evidence until closure criteria are met.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m13','An access request passes preventive SoD because the requested entitlement is not yet present in the imported entitlement catalog. What control gap does this indicate?','["Too many reviewers","Incomplete or stale entitlement inventory/mapping feeding the risk model","The user has no profile photo","The notification expired"]',1,'Preventive analysis is only as complete as the entitlement inventory and risk mappings. Validate import freshness and catalog coverage.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m14','A REST connector's next-page token expires during a long-running import. What is the most reliable recovery design?','["Restart from page one without deduplication","Persist checkpoints where supported, refresh authentication, restart from a safe cursor and make ingestion idempotent","Skip all remaining pages","Treat token expiry as successful completion"]',1,'Checkpointed, idempotent imports can recover from token expiry without silently skipping or duplicating records.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m15','An application owner disputes a certification revoke because the entitlement is required for emergency support. What is the appropriate governance path?','["Ignore the reviewer decision","Use a documented exception/mitigating control with owner, justification, expiry and periodic reassessment","Permanently exempt all users","Delete the certification record"]',1,'Exceptions should be time-bound, owned, justified and reassessed; they must not erase the review decision or audit trail.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m16','A production cutover imports accounts correctly but provisions duplicate accounts for users with pre-existing target accounts. Which implementation control should be validated?','["Email template subject","Account correlation/reconciliation and create-vs-update provisioning logic before enabling writes","Training completion percentage","Quiz randomization"]',1,'Before write operations, validate account correlation and reconciliation so existing target accounts are updated rather than recreated.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m17','A nightly import and a mover workflow update the same identity concurrently, producing inconsistent access decisions. What is the best design response?','["Run more imports concurrently","Review job orchestration, event ordering, idempotency and locking/serialization for identity recalculation","Remove all mover rules","Allow last-write-wins without monitoring"]',1,'Concurrent processing must have deterministic ordering and idempotent recalculation to avoid conflicting access decisions.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m18','An audit requires proof that a privileged entitlement was removed from the target, not merely that a revoke decision was recorded. Which evidence is strongest?','["Certification decision alone","Remediation task completion plus connector/target response or independent target-side verification timestamped to the account","A screenshot of the dashboard KPI","A manager statement"]',1,'The review decision proves intent; completed remediation and target-side evidence demonstrate actual access removal.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m19','A connector works from a developer laptop but fails from the Saviynt execution environment with connection timeout. What should be compared?','["Developer browser cache","Runtime network route, firewall allowlists, DNS, proxy, TLS trust and source IP from the execution environment","Question difficulty","Identity display name"]',1,'Connectivity must be tested from the actual execution environment; workstation success does not prove runtime network reachability.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m20','A team wants to rotate a connector service credential with no outage. Which approach is safest?','["Replace the credential without coordination","Use overlapping credential validity where supported, update the secure secret, test authentication, then revoke the old credential and monitor jobs","Email the password to all admins","Disable connector authentication"]',1,'A controlled overlap and verification window minimizes downtime; secrets must remain in approved secret storage, not code or logs.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m21','A certification population filter excludes users whose manager attribute is null, including critical privileged accounts. What should be done?','["Keep excluding them","Create an exception/alternate reviewer assignment path for missing manager data and report data-quality exceptions","Cancel all reviews","Set every manager to the same user"]',1,'Missing manager data must not silently remove high-risk access from review; provide alternate ownership and remediation.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m22','A role assignment grants an entitlement that violates SoD only when combined with an existing birthright role. What must the risk evaluation consider?','["Only the newly requested role in isolation","The user's effective access across existing and proposed roles/entitlements","Only the requester's department name","Only direct entitlements"]',1,'SoD analysis must evaluate cumulative effective access, including inherited, birthright and newly requested access.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m23','An API returns HTTP 200 but includes per-record errors in the response body. The connector marks the entire import successful. What is missing?','["A new endpoint","Response-level validation and record-level error handling with accurate job reconciliation","A longer certification period","A user notification banner"]',1,'HTTP status alone is insufficient. Parse application-level results, capture rejected records and report partial failures accurately.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m24','A custom analytics control returns duplicate users after joining identity, account and entitlement datasets. What is the most likely SQL correction?','["Remove all joins","Review join cardinality and aggregate/deduplicate at the intended identity/account grain before counting","Use SELECT * only","Sort by display name"]',1,'One-to-many joins multiply rows. Define the reporting grain and aggregate or use distinct keys before computing metrics.','Advanced',true,'advanced'),
('m25','A go-live plan proposes enabling all provisioning jobs immediately after the first successful import. What is the strongest readiness gate?','["A successful login by the project lead","Validated correlation, entitlement catalog, access mappings, provisioning tests, negative tests, rollback plan, owner sign-off and monitoring","A completed slide deck","A successful email notification"]',1,'Provisioning should be enabled only after end-to-end controls and operational readiness are demonstrated and approved.','Advanced',true,'advanced');
